.TH COF 1 "2026-11-13" "cof 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cof \- run, check and manage Circuitry orchestrations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
cof [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
cof is Circuitry's command-line interface: it runs, validates, inspects,
generates, lists, and manages orchestration documents and their configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
Print version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Validate an orchestration file against the schema. (alias of \fBvalidate\fR)
.TP
.B doctor
System diagnostics \(em check backends, config, and connectivity.
.TP
.B eject
Copy a bundled orchestration to the current directory for editing.
.TP
.B fetch
Fetch a shared library orchestration.
.TP
.B gen
Generate an orchestration from a natural language prompt, single-shot. Drives
\fBagents/meta_orchestrator.yml\fR. For a multi-turn, clarifying-questions
build instead, see \fBcof wizard\fR.
.TP
.B info
Show details for a bundled orchestration.
.TP
.B init
Initialize a new circuitry project in the current directory.
.TP
.B inspect
Show orchestration metadata.
.TP
.B library
Manage library sources (\fBruntime.library.sources\fR).
.TP
.B list
List available bundled orchestrations (compiled-in extensions with
--extensions, an adapter's models with --models <adapter>).
.TP
.B man
Show a cof man page through man, or print its roff when piped or given --roff.
.TP
.B mcp
Run the circuitry MCP server (stdio transport).
.TP
.B run
Execute an orchestration.
.TP
.B run-library
Fetch and run a shared library orchestration.
.TP
.B score
Preview per-effect complexity scores for an orchestration without running it.
.TP
.B setup
Interactive setup wizard \(em detect backends, configure model, and create
config.
.TP
.B trust
Trust a project config file, or consent to an orchestration document's
capabilities. A .yml/.yaml PATH is a document (shows the capabilities it needs
and asks); anything else is a project config file (shows what it sets and
asks).
.TP
.B tui
Launch the terminal UI (requires the 'tui' extra).
.TP
.B untrust
Stop applying a project config file you trusted.
.TP
.B validate
Validate an orchestration file against the schema. (alias: check)
.TP
.B version
Print version. (also: \fBcof --version\fR)
.TP
.B wizard
Build an orchestration by talking to the wizard, headlessly; unlike \fBcof
gen\fR, it asks clarifying questions.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_CONFIG
An explicit config JSON path (same as --config). When set, replaces the global
config and any project config entirely, rather than layering on top of them.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_MODEL
Overrides the resolved config's default_model.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ADAPTER
Overrides the resolved config's default_adapter.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ADAPTER_URL
Overrides the resolved default adapter's base_url.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_COMFYUI_URL
Overrides the comfyui plugin's base_url.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_SYSTEMONE_URL
Overrides the systemone plugin's base_url.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_ADAPTERS
Comma-separated allowlist, narrowing (never widening) the resolved config's
enabled_adapters.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_PLUGINS
Comma-separated allowlist, narrowing (never widening) the resolved config's
enabled_plugins.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_TOOLS
Comma-separated allowlist, narrowing (never widening) the resolved config's
enabled_tools.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENVIRONMENT
Overrides the resolved config's environment (dev, prod, or test).
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_TRUST_PROJECT_CONFIG
Trusts a project config in the current directory without running cof trust
first.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/config.json
The global config, applied first; a trusted project config layers on top of
it.
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/.env
Private environment variables, loaded before config resolution (written by cof
setup).
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/trusted.json
Project configs trusted by cof trust; config resolution consults it before
applying a discovered project config.
.TP
.I ./circuitry.config.json, ./config.json
A project config in the working directory, layered on top of the global config
once trusted.
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/services/
Background service state (cof's service tooling).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed, or the input was invalid.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error -- an unrecognized option or missing argument.
